{
  "_comment": [
    "Maps each source dataset's own class indices onto our taxonomy.",
    "Indices are positions in that dataset's data.yaml 'names' list.",
    "Targets: shahed | bird | helicopter | other | drop.",
    "",
    "'drop' marks a whole dataset that is not Shahed data at all. These were",
    "pulled in by a text search on the Roboflow project name and would",
    "otherwise poison the pool -- sinakhoshgoftar is 2,473 crowd photographs",
    "whose only class is 'person' (the OWNER is named Shahed), and",
    "roopa-khilare labels the interceptor drone, not the target it intercepts.",
    "",
    "Datasets whose classes are unnamed ('0'/'1') are kept only where the",
    "content has been visually confirmed; all three such datasets here were",
    "confirmed to be renders, so their boxes are shahed-class but synthetic."
  ],

